# Ancient Vendetta: "Choose a card name. Search target opponent's graveyard, hand, and library for up to four cards with that name
# and exile them. Then that player shuffles." Bot2 holds six Ornithopters: one in its graveyard (discarded to hand size at the end
# of turn 2), two in its hand, three in its library. Bot1 names Ornithopter as the spell resolves and finds, in the order the text
# names the zones, the one in the graveyard, both in the hand and only one in the library - four in all, the limit - leaving two in
# the library even though they were there to find (the ruling: "you may only search for up to four cards with the chosen name, even if
# you find more of them"). The Islands in every zone are untouched.

